  "notes": [
   "Phi_k(u,v) = N_k(u) - v*D_k(u) is LINEAR in v, so it is irreducible iff gcd(N_k, D_k) = 1 in QQ[u]; factor() calls verify this explicitly for k<=8.",
   "deg N_k = k^2 means the rational map x o [k] has degree k^2; the relation between u and v is a rational function (deg_v = 1), so the obstruction shows up as the u-degree / total degree k^2.",
   "Degrees are characteristic-independent for large p (lc N_k = 1, lc D_k = k^2); F_p run verifies the formulas against actual scalar multiplication."
  ]
